<chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude"  xml:id="chap_the-derivative_chap_the-derivative">
  <title>The Derivative</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>
      In developing the <m>S</m>-<m>I</m>-<m>R</m> model in chapter 1 we took the idea of the rate of change of a population as intuitively clear.
      The rate at which one quantity changes with respect to another is a central concept of calculus and leads to a broad range of insights.
      The chief purpose of this chapter is to develop a fuller understanding<mdash/>both analytic and geometric<mdash/>of the connection between a function and its rate of change.
      To do this we will introduce the concept of the <em> derivative</em>
          <idx><h>derivative</h></idx>
      of a function.
    </p>
  </introduction>
